IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `act-provisions`
IMPORT `act-xrefs`

-- Tests for act-provisions.l4 and act-xrefs.l4.
-- One assertion per row of `the cross-references`.
-- A row of a section, chapter, part, division, schedule, table or the dictionary passes when the cited identifier is in the provision index,
-- when the heading the row carries is the index's heading for it (and the heading printed with the citation, when there is one, is the same),
-- when the row's marking of the target as in scope or out of scope is the index's, and when the pinpoint, if there is one, names a sub-provision the section has.
-- A row to another Act or instrument passes when it names the instrument and its target is marked `not resolved here`.

§ `Tests: cross-references`

GIVEN r IS A `Cross-reference`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the row checks out` MEANS
    CONSIDER r's `kind`
    WHEN `to another Act or instrument` THEN
        r's `target` EQUALS `not resolved here` AND NOT (r's `cited identifier` EQUALS "")
    WHEN `to a provision of the section or definition it is in` THEN
        `the heading of the provision` (r's `cited identifier`) EQUALS JUST (r's `heading of the cited provision`)
        AND r's `target` EQUALS `in scope`
        AND (r's `pinpoint path` EQUALS "" OR `the section has the sub-provision` (r's `cited identifier`) (r's `pinpoint path`))
    OTHERWISE
        `the heading of the provision` (r's `cited identifier`) EQUALS JUST (r's `heading of the cited provision`)
        AND (r's `heading printed with the citation` EQUALS "" OR r's `heading printed with the citation` EQUALS r's `heading of the cited provision`)
        AND `the marking of the target agrees with the index` r
        AND (r's `pinpoint path` EQUALS "" OR `the section has the sub-provision` (r's `cited identifier`) (r's `pinpoint path`))

GIVEN r IS A `Cross-reference`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the marking of the target agrees with the index` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the provision is in scope` (r's `cited identifier`)
    WHEN JUST inScope THEN
        IF   inScope
        THEN r's `target` EQUALS `in scope`
        ELSE r's `target` EQUALS `out of scope`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE

GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the row numbered` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the row found` n `the cross-references`
    WHEN JUST r THEN `the row checks out` r
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE

GIVEN n IS A NUMBER, rs IS A LIST OF `Cross-reference`
GIVETH A MAYBE `Cross-reference`
`the row found` MEANS
    CONSIDER rs
    WHEN EMPTY THEN NOTHING
    WHEN first FOLLOWED BY rest THEN
        IF   first's `row` EQUALS n
        THEN JUST first
        ELSE `the row found` n rest


